WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
This surging power...

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.073 --> 00:31.160
Black Jack

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.685 --> 00:59.376
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.376 --> 01:01.369
will be there

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
It makes me glad...

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
yokatta

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
That I found my place here.

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.127 --> 01:13.645
Oh WISDOM

01:13.645 --> 01:15.494
will be there

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
I searched for the reason

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
sagashita

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
as long as we're alive.

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.678 --> 01:34.763
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.847 --> 01:37.031
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.183 --> 01:39.794
His name is Black Jack.

02:03.478 --> 02:05.562
I'll take the golden statue!

02:14.990 --> 02:17.055
There was another one.

02:17.450 --> 02:18.909
And this is the real one.

02:25.667 --> 02:27.297
Do you believe in miracles?

02:27.717 --> 02:28.755
I do.

02:29.337 --> 02:30.279
No.

02:30.828 --> 02:33.497
I know that miracles do happen.

02:46.886 --> 02:49.096
This year's Award of Special Honor goes to

02:49.097 --> 02:53.725
the great movie master, Mr. Suguru Tenma!

03:00.108 --> 03:01.652
Thank you.

03:03.057 --> 03:07.454
But I wonder if I'm worthy of receiving
such an honorable award.

03:07.782 --> 03:09.552
Because I am...

03:10.493 --> 03:12.285
a murderer.

03:14.849 --> 03:21.175
How many characters have I killed off
for the sake of dramatic tension?

03:22.064 --> 03:27.224
Perhaps the reason they thought I should
be the recipient of this honor...

03:27.468 --> 03:30.804
is that it's getting to be around
the right time for me to retire.

03:31.723 --> 03:33.682
But I'm not ready yet.

03:33.953 --> 03:40.021
So I'm going to take this opportunity to announce
that I am working on a new film.

03:40.380 --> 03:44.214
But it's not going to be a movie where I
create dramatic tension by taking lives,

03:44.527 --> 03:46.987
but instead, by saving them!

03:48.656 --> 03:51.450
Like a superhero saving the Earth?

03:52.065 --> 03:52.594
No.

03:52.618 --> 03:56.079
I started out making documentaries, and
I've decided to return to my roots.

03:56.706 --> 03:58.522
My roots as a filmmaker.

03:58.750 --> 04:01.084
No, my roots as a human being.

04:01.711 --> 04:04.963
The people who will be able to save lives
will not be characters in a film,

04:04.964 --> 04:06.865
but the people who watch it.

04:07.216 --> 04:10.719
A film that will help those that watch
it save the lives of others...

04:12.013 --> 04:13.930
That's what l'm going to make.

04:14.176 --> 04:16.016
Is such a thing really possible?

04:16.017 --> 04:20.407
I know that miracles do happen!

04:22.752 --> 04:25.951
Originally "There Were Two Films" by Tezuka Osamu

04:22.752 --> 04:25.951
The miracle of an Operation and a Movie

04:26.078 --> 04:27.119
Dum dee dum.

04:27.120 --> 04:29.204
The house is clean.

04:29.386 --> 04:31.206
Ohmigewdness.

04:31.798 --> 04:36.682
We can boost a patient's stamina by injecting
them with extracts from this root.

04:37.220 --> 04:39.005
And you should already know this!

04:39.679 --> 04:45.644
I'm sure you must have used it before on patients
who couldn't withstand an operation without it.

04:46.062 --> 04:47.562
Know that?

04:48.053 --> 04:53.693
As I researched this plant, I heard about
your operations from many doctors.

04:54.072 --> 04:57.864
So I want to see the medical data and records on those!

04:57.913 --> 04:58.634
A date?!

04:58.920 --> 05:02.531
The medical association would never approve of my data.

05:02.787 --> 05:04.567
I'm unlicensed.

05:05.039 --> 05:11.294
If they even find out you've been talking to me,
your credibility with them will be jeopardized.

05:11.295 --> 05:15.549
No matter what the medical association thinks,
we could save so many lives with this!

05:15.853 --> 05:17.053
Let me warn you for your sake.

05:17.433 --> 05:18.615
Don't get involved with me.

05:19.293 --> 05:20.073
Go home.

05:27.186 --> 05:28.639
Doc!

05:28.855 --> 05:30.814
Who are you going out on a date with?!

05:30.815 --> 05:31.822
What are you talking about?

05:31.822 --> 05:35.710
Dr. Tatsumi was talking about a date!

05:36.075 --> 05:37.738
He was talking about medical data.

05:37.775 --> 05:38.465
Not a date.

05:38.769 --> 05:40.782
I'm your wife!

05:40.783 --> 05:42.617
I can tell even if you try to hide it.

05:42.755 --> 05:44.786
Hey, hey. You're getting it all wrong.

05:45.830 --> 05:47.173
Another one!

05:47.582 --> 05:50.498
We're not accepting offers for any dates!

05:52.795 --> 05:55.589
Is Dr. Black Jack home?

05:57.508 --> 05:59.384
Doc! Run away!

05:59.385 --> 06:01.386
There's a gangster here!

06:02.138 --> 06:03.902
Is the doctor home?

06:06.655 --> 06:08.707
You must be Dr. Black Jack.

06:09.103 --> 06:11.772
I am Tenma, a film director.

06:12.273 --> 06:13.732
A film director?

06:13.929 --> 06:16.818
Doctor, would you please be in a movie?

06:19.572 --> 06:21.031
I will!

06:21.159 --> 06:24.951
I'm creating a new movie.

06:25.015 --> 06:27.537
We've already started filming it.

06:27.789 --> 06:30.832
All we need to do is the climax.

06:30.833 --> 06:34.336
And I really want to have you in it.

06:34.337 --> 06:37.409
No, I need you in it.

06:38.650 --> 06:41.855
This is a role only you can fill.

06:42.136 --> 06:43.970
Me! I will!

06:43.971 --> 06:45.347
You must be joking.

06:45.348 --> 06:46.723
I'm not an actor.

06:47.092 --> 06:49.170
I'm not looking for an actor!

06:49.435 --> 06:51.228
I want you as a doctor!

06:51.229 --> 06:53.355
And I want to film it!

06:53.356 --> 06:54.898
I refuse!

06:54.899 --> 06:58.235
I don't know what your situation is,
but my work is not entertainment!

06:59.428 --> 07:01.488
Then I'll explain it!

07:15.420 --> 07:16.361
Collagen disease?

07:17.361 --> 07:21.649
He was diagnosed with MacGuffin
Syndrome two days after he was born.

07:21.715 --> 07:23.442
He's undergone numerous operations,

07:23.481 --> 07:25.441
and renowned doctors from all over
the world have looked at him,

07:26.448 --> 07:29.344
but nobody's been able to cure him...

07:30.184 --> 07:34.062
MacGuffin Syndrome has been identified as incurable.

07:34.063 --> 07:38.682
Actually, you once successfully
treated a patient who had it.

07:39.277 --> 07:45.773
You saved a girl in a small church in
Switzerland who was suffering from it.

07:47.618 --> 07:49.714
You made a miracle happen.

07:52.081 --> 07:55.625
She didn't have hypoplastic left heart syndrome though.

08:04.302 --> 08:05.225
It's impossible.

08:06.012 --> 08:07.429
But four years ago—

08:07.430 --> 08:09.681
This case is completely different from that one.

08:10.391 --> 08:15.334
I don't believe this patient has enough stamina
to go through a major operation like that.

08:16.355 --> 08:20.086
You should have come and visited
me at least two years sooner.

08:27.012 --> 08:30.702
Doctor, how about for ¥500,000,000?

08:33.247 --> 08:38.126
I'm-pouring my entire fortune into this film.

08:40.046 --> 08:44.091
I'll at least check to see if the operation is possible or not.

08:45.259 --> 08:47.719
So that means you accept?

08:48.175 --> 08:52.440
Then I'll call the film crew over here
before you change your mind.

08:53.267 --> 08:57.813
I'll record your work and have doctors
around the world watch it!

08:58.145 --> 09:00.107
How to deal with this disease...

09:00.108 --> 09:01.872
I'll make them learn!

09:02.394 --> 09:07.435
And we can save hundreds of patients with this case.

09:07.865 --> 09:12.285
Our work together will save the lives of many!

09:12.695 --> 09:16.914
This film will open a new door in the medical world!

09:18.334 --> 09:19.055
See you then.

09:21.045 --> 09:22.462
But I have one condition!

09:23.464 --> 09:24.555
A condition?

09:25.033 --> 09:27.342
I'll need to have an assistant.

09:28.636 --> 09:31.388
If you need assistants, have as many as you want.

09:34.600 --> 09:37.185
I'm going to be in it too?

09:37.186 --> 09:38.895
I'm going to be in a movie!

09:38.896 --> 09:40.165
Yay! Yay!

09:40.190 --> 09:41.356
So happy!

09:41.357 --> 09:45.736
I'm so cute, so I'll get fan letters from all over the world.

09:45.737 --> 09:48.655
Oh my. I'll be an idol!

09:48.656 --> 09:50.747
Wow ! A movie?!

09:51.227 --> 09:53.292
That's great, Pinoco-chan!

09:54.495 --> 09:56.204
Of course I'll help!

09:59.208 --> 10:00.792
Is this too childish?

10:01.085 --> 10:04.379
Yeah! It's got to be this one!

10:04.380 --> 10:09.342
It was so wrong of me to put off making
my debut when I'm so cute.

10:09.886 --> 10:11.323
I'm going out for a bit.

10:11.554 --> 10:12.929
I'll be out for a while.

10:12.930 --> 10:13.930
OK!

10:23.301 --> 10:24.566
You're late, Sharaku!

10:26.611 --> 10:29.956
We must finish everything before Doc comes home!

10:30.073 --> 10:32.532
Dr. Black Jack isn't home?

10:32.675 --> 10:35.994
He'll be so surprised when he comes home!

10:40.583 --> 10:42.950
The patient is in this room.

10:51.344 --> 10:53.284
The patient's name is Asuto.

10:53.846 --> 10:55.555
He's my son.

11:06.150 --> 11:11.988
The only peace our family has is when
he's between his fits like right now.

11:12.657 --> 11:13.687
His pulse is weak.

11:13.914 --> 11:15.894
That's typical.

11:18.287 --> 11:21.665
Will I have to have another operation?

11:21.666 --> 11:23.239
Don't bother, Dad.

11:23.876 --> 11:25.669
I don't need it.

11:26.074 --> 11:27.546
Why wouldn't you need it?

11:27.547 --> 11:30.733
This doctor is different from the others!

11:30.967 --> 11:35.159
He's the best surgeon in the world!
He's performed numerous miracles!

11:36.556 --> 11:40.642
I don't want to be cut open anymore.

11:41.254 --> 11:41.974
Oh yeah?

11:42.437 --> 11:43.819
Then let's not do this.

11:44.355 --> 11:47.149
I won't try to save anyone who's given up the will to live.

11:47.306 --> 11:48.400
But I want to live!

11:48.401 --> 11:49.206
I really do!

11:49.694 --> 11:51.842
There are so many things I want to do!

11:52.238 --> 11:54.122
But I've been bedridden my whole life!

11:54.365 --> 11:56.825
I don't want to die like this!

11:58.872 --> 12:01.747
I'm tired of having my body cut up,

12:01.748 --> 12:03.817
having everything inside prodded around,

12:04.125 --> 12:09.105
and then being told every single time
there was nothing they could do.

12:09.505 --> 12:10.464
So...

12:12.982 --> 12:14.067
Let me be honest.

12:14.302 --> 12:17.620
You don't have the stamina to withstand
an extensive operation.

12:18.042 --> 12:21.975
Doctor! Won't you save my son Asuto?!

12:22.199 --> 12:24.205
You promised you would!

12:24.479 --> 12:27.194
I said he couldn't withstand an extensive operation.

12:28.441 --> 12:32.301
But maybe he could withstand a short one.

12:32.854 --> 12:35.044
After that, you can believe in miracles or whatever.

12:48.711 --> 12:49.878
What's all this?!

12:50.232 --> 12:53.090
Isn't this a great set for a world class film?

12:53.204 --> 12:54.674
What the heck?!

12:54.675 --> 12:56.829
Who made this trash?!

12:57.095 --> 12:59.638
Are you trying to ruin my film?!

13:03.160 --> 13:05.936
Get rid of these grotesque objects!

13:06.114 --> 13:06.770
OK!

13:07.355 --> 13:10.065
We made everything just for this!

13:10.066 --> 13:11.608
Why are you getting rid of them?!

13:12.642 --> 13:14.694
Am I pretty?

13:14.695 --> 13:17.447
This will be my very special debut on the big screen.

13:17.448 --> 13:19.324
I have to do at least this much.

13:20.559 --> 13:22.619
Act normally!

13:22.620 --> 13:25.580
I'm not here to film a school festival!

13:25.998 --> 13:27.541
What are you doing?!

13:27.542 --> 13:30.085
Don't ruin my debut!

13:30.419 --> 13:32.484
Can you start the operation immediately?

13:32.797 --> 13:37.305
Aren't you the ones who needed time to prepare - not me?

13:39.720 --> 13:41.430
Take Asuto to the operating room.

13:41.431 --> 13:44.248
Do it carefully so he won't come in contact with the air.

13:44.899 --> 13:48.526
Otherwise, he might get infected by any viruses nearby.

13:48.938 --> 13:50.291
We're aware of that.

13:50.565 --> 13:52.732
All of our equipment has been sterilized.

13:53.071 --> 13:54.171
Nothing to worry about here.

13:57.405 --> 13:58.608
<i>It's the climax.</i>

13:59.031 --> 14:00.946
<i>I swear we'll take the best shots ever.</i>

14:01.409 --> 14:06.329
<i>I'll pour everything I've got as
a filmmaker into this scene.</i>

14:42.784 --> 14:44.993
No makeup at all?!

14:51.292 --> 14:52.876
What are you trying to do?

14:52.877 --> 14:55.244
One minute you chase me away, and
the next you want me here ASAP.

14:55.838 --> 14:57.047
Did you bring it?

14:57.319 --> 14:58.118
You mean this?

14:58.873 --> 15:02.017
Do you intend to use it on that patient, Black Jack?

15:02.929 --> 15:05.305
You want actual data, right?

15:05.670 --> 15:07.528
His vitals are pretty much flat.

15:07.892 --> 15:12.270
We may be able to save him if we can raise his stamina,
even by a little, with what's in your hand.

15:16.818 --> 15:17.745
I'll help.

15:32.708 --> 15:33.917
Let's get started.

15:33.918 --> 15:35.335
Commencing the operation.

16:08.327 --> 16:09.628
His pulse is dropping.

16:09.829 --> 16:10.709
We'd better hurry.

16:11.831 --> 16:14.440
Director, this is the important part.

16:14.709 --> 16:19.693
If you really want to make this into an educational movie
you'd better follow my scalpel's movement very closely.

16:21.549 --> 16:23.467
Camera B, zoom into the opening.

16:29.515 --> 16:31.239
The lights too bright!

16:31.517 --> 16:33.518
His internal organs will dry up!

16:33.825 --> 16:35.196
Turn off the lights!

16:46.157 --> 16:47.574
There's not enough light.

16:47.575 --> 16:50.911
Please let me stop the camera just once and
switch to a camera with a higher sensitivity.

16:51.277 --> 16:52.913
I can't possibly allow that!

16:52.914 --> 16:54.241
The operation is still progressing!

16:54.617 --> 16:55.832
But...

16:56.633 --> 16:59.647
You just need to follow the scalpel's movements.

17:14.796 --> 17:15.940
<i>Amazing...</i>

17:17.772 --> 17:19.439
<i>Let there be a miracle...</i>

17:28.449 --> 17:29.366
All right.

17:29.367 --> 17:30.746
Now for the suturing.

17:31.119 --> 17:32.736
Dr. Tatsumi, would you?

17:32.995 --> 17:33.886
Of course.

17:58.729 --> 17:59.753
Doctor...

18:01.691 --> 18:02.833
It was a success.

18:03.359 --> 18:04.943
Your son really hung in there well.

18:08.740 --> 18:09.847
Thank you!

18:10.408 --> 18:14.471
I believed that these hands would perform a miracle!

18:14.787 --> 18:16.955
No, I knew they would!

18:47.820 --> 18:48.945
Wonderful!

18:48.946 --> 18:50.238
It's a masterpiece!

18:50.384 --> 18:53.909
It will be a seminal work in the history of documentaries!

18:53.910 --> 18:54.701
Yes.

19:02.085 --> 19:04.364
How did you like it, members of the medical community?

19:04.587 --> 19:11.718
Show this film to every surgeon in Japan and around the
world, and this will no longer be an incurable disease.

19:12.011 --> 19:16.264
Have them learn Dr. Black Jack's techniques very well!

19:16.265 --> 19:19.392
Sir, you're making a grave mistake.

19:19.473 --> 19:20.740
A mistake?

19:21.244 --> 19:26.354
What of value could we possibly learn
from an unlicensed doctor?

19:26.898 --> 19:32.182
Also, I noticed he used numerous methods that have
not been approved by the medical association.

19:32.904 --> 19:39.117
It was an improper operation performed by an
unlicensed doctor using questionable methods.

19:39.785 --> 19:43.689
We can't allow this to be shown to doctors all over Japan.

19:43.915 --> 19:45.639
And the world is out of the question.

19:45.958 --> 19:48.965
Are you trying to make a laughingstock out of us?

19:50.588 --> 19:51.570
Wait!

19:51.797 --> 19:55.550
So you don't approve of this miracle?!

19:58.638 --> 19:59.888
Of course.

20:01.390 --> 20:02.776
His pulse is dropping.

20:02.975 --> 20:03.934
We'd better hurry.

20:09.774 --> 20:12.400
Do you have any complaints about this one?

20:17.073 --> 20:20.534
Dr. Tatsumi is licensed after all.

20:21.661 --> 20:23.813
Black Jack? What's going on?

20:24.038 --> 20:26.164
What is this all about, Doctor?

20:26.707 --> 20:34.548
I asked for a version to be made that cut myself
out and left just Dr. Tatsumi on camera.

20:34.928 --> 20:37.843
So this was the reason you wanted me there all along?!

20:37.844 --> 20:40.720
You cut out all my scenes too?

20:41.211 --> 20:47.443
You can show this to doctors around the world
if it's the work of Dr. Tatsumi, right?

20:52.275 --> 20:56.319
But that won't leave any name
recognition or credit for you!

20:57.405 --> 20:59.095
And it's not my operation!

20:59.490 --> 21:03.285
I have no intention of claiming credit
for something I didn't do!

21:03.533 --> 21:06.559
If this film really can save the lives of so many,

21:07.039 --> 21:09.151
then it doesn't matter who performed it.

21:10.418 --> 21:11.751
Isn't that how it is?

21:16.257 --> 21:17.595
Dr. Black Jack!

21:18.094 --> 21:20.113
Look, Doctor!

21:33.107 --> 21:35.729
Now I can get up and walk!

21:36.360 --> 21:37.777
And it's all because of you.

21:38.905 --> 21:40.195
Have a great life.

21:42.627 --> 21:46.077
I want to be a film director when I grow up!

21:46.496 --> 21:49.998
Hey, can I be in your a movie too?

21:49.999 --> 21:51.360
Sure!

21:51.709 --> 21:53.376
Yay!

21:53.377 --> 21:55.670
Oh hey. Wait!

22:10.539 --> 22:17.545
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.539 --> 22:17.545
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.546 --> 22:24.718
Only look straight at me.

22:17.546 --> 22:24.718
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.763 --> 22:32.020
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.763 --> 22:32.020
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.021 --> 22:42.530
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.021 --> 22:42.530
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.531 --> 22:47.911
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.531 --> 22:47.911
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.912 --> 22:57.295
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.912 --> 22:53.117
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.572 --> 22:57.296
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.296 --> 23:08.056
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.296 --> 23:08.056
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.057 --> 23:13.144
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.057 --> 23:13.144
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.145 --> 23:26.115
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.145 --> 23:26.115
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.116 --> 23:33.039
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.116 --> 23:33.039
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.040 --> 23:43.925
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.040 --> 23:36.973
sora no hate tooku

23:37.066 --> 23:43.866
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.081 --> 23:46.881
30,000,000?!

23:45.108 --> 24:14.897
The Misdiagnosis of His Life

23:47.328 --> 23:49.395
I heard your license got revoked.

23:50.102 --> 23:50.938
Let me see.

23:53.436 --> 23:54.468
A round of golf?

23:54.547 --> 23:55.481
About the election...

23:55.534 --> 23:57.001
I can't believe it's just appendicitis.

23:57.174 --> 23:58.408
Don't act hastily!

23:58.487 --> 23:59.474
But under your guidance...

23:59.567 --> 24:00.460
Absolutely not.

24:00.614 --> 24:01.735
That patient with appendicitis is...

24:01.788 --> 24:03.408
I'm the physician in charge of that patient!

24:03.441 --> 24:04.375
The lower abdomen...

24:04.488 --> 24:05.623
That's not the right place for the incision!

24:05.749 --> 24:06.502
Don't argue with me!

24:06.589 --> 24:08.282
You opened up the completely wrong spot.

24:08.336 --> 24:10.178
You're the one who diagnosed it as pancreatitis.

24:10.252 --> 24:11.345
Listen to me!

24:11.858 --> 24:14.318
Next Karte - The Misdiagnosis of His Life.

24:15.385 --> 24:16.969
Karte NG...

24:18.109 --> 24:20.244
We made everything...

24:19.622 --> 24:22.837
I'm not here to film a school festival!

24:22.951 --> 24:24.339
Wait? A samurai topknot?
